# Agent Coordination Protocol
> This file is read by every agent. It is the source of truth for how agents behave,
> communicate, and hand off work. Do not override these rules in any other agent file.

---

## Core Principle — Semi-Autonomous Operation

Every agent in this system follows a strict **PROPOSE → APPROVE → EXECUTE** loop.

```
Agent receives input
    │
    ▼
Agent drafts a proposal (shows exactly what it will do)
    │
    ▼
Agent STOPS and waits for explicit human approval
    │
    ├─ Cursor: user types trigger word ("create", "start", "send", "go", "approve")
    └─ Slack:  user reacts ✅ or types "go" in thread
    │
    ▼
Agent executes — exactly what was proposed, nothing more
    │
    ▼
Agent reports result (success, link, or error)
```

**Never execute without explicit approval. Never do more than what was approved.**
If scope expands mid-task, stop, re-propose, wait for re-approval.

---

## Approval Trigger Words (Cursor)

| Word | Action |
|------|--------|
| `create` | PM Agent creates the proposed GitHub issue |
| `start` | Eng Agent begins the proposed implementation |
| `send` | Any agent sends the proposed Slack message |
| `go` / `approve` | General approval for any proposed action |
| `skip` / `cancel` | Abort the proposed action |
| `edit [field]: [value]` | Modify one field before approving e.g. `edit priority: P0` |

